{"q":"119","t":"Pascal's Triangle II","d":"Easy","p":false,"c":"<p>Given an integer <code>rowIndex</code>, return the <code>rowIndex<sup>th</sup></code> (<strong>0-indexed</strong>) row of the <strong>Pascal&#39;s triangle</strong>.</p>\n\n<p>In <strong>Pascal&#39;s triangle</strong>, each number is the sum of the two numbers directly above it as shown:</p>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"/assets/img/ccbdd7dde75a8496.gif\" style=\"height:240px; width:260px\" />\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> rowIndex = 3\n<strong>Output:</strong> [1,3,3,1]\n</pre><p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> rowIndex = 0\n<strong>Output:</strong> [1]\n</pre><p><strong class=\"example\">Example 3:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> rowIndex = 1\n<strong>Output:</strong> [1,1]\n</pre>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>0 &lt;= rowIndex &lt;= 33</code></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Follow up:</strong> Could you optimize your algorithm to use only <code>O(rowIndex)</code> extra space?</p>\n","h":[],"m":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"getRow\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"rowIndex\",\r\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"list<integer>\"\r\n  }\r\n}","g":[{"name":"Array","slug":"array"},{"name":"Dynamic Programming","slug":"dynamic-programming"}],"s":[{"t":"Pascal's Triangle","s":"pascals-triangle","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Find Triangular Sum of an Array","s":"find-triangular-sum-of-an-array","d":"Medium","p":false}],"co":[["Google","google"],["Microsoft","microsoft"],["Amazon","amazon"]]}